# Go dependency floors applied to mongo-tools by scripts/mongo_tools_builder.sh
# (--get_sources), between `git clone` and `go mod tidy && go mod vendor`.
#
# Editing this file plus bumping --release is the whole point of this repo: it makes a
# tools-only security rebuild a minutes-long job instead of a full PSMDB rebuild.
#
# GET: minimum versions, to clear CVEs. A module is bumped only when upstream pins it
#   lower; if upstream is already at or above the floor it is left alone, so building a
#   newer tag never downgrades anything. The build log says `keep` or `bump` per module.
# DROP_REPLACE: upstream `replace` directives to remove first. Neither 100.18.0 nor
#   100.19.1 has any, so it is a no-op kept verbatim from psmdb_builder.sh.
#
# Values are PSMDB-2259 ("Update go and libs to fix CVEs"), as in psmdb_builder.sh on
# release-7.0.43-23 / v8.0 / v8.3. Against 100.18.0 all four are bumps; 100.19.1 already
# pins newer versions of all four, so there every one is a `keep`.

GO_DEPS_DROP_REPLACE="golang.org/x/crypto@v0.45.0 golang.org/x/net@v0.47.0 golang.org/x/text@v0.31.0 github.com/klauspost/compress@v1.17.8"

GO_DEPS_GET="golang.org/x/crypto@v0.56.0 golang.org/x/net@v0.57.0 golang.org/x/text@v0.41.0 github.com/klauspost/compress@v1.18.7"
